13306	{"artifactId":"LLD-008e146ad1475ef9-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-008e146ad1475ef9-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-10T13:43:54.725Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The bounded wait and the handed measure address root causes 1 and 3 of the ISSUE at the place they occur: one wait in measureConnection covers both the single-source and the pool path, and the context builder gets a way to be handed the run's measure.","evidence":"src/analyze/measure.ts:444-494: measureConnection is the only function that awaits `pool.acquire(id)` (456) and the unbounded listings `r.listTables({ complete: true })` (466), `k.listNamespaces({ complete: true })` (476), `listFilesForConnection` (484). measureDataSource calls it at 438; measureDataPool calls it directly at 512 (`await measureConnection(pool, id, undefined)`), not through measureDataSource, as the design says. No signal or timer exists anywhere in the file today. src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1372-1378 reads only `{ intent, sizeHint }` from the input and always measures, so it has no way to be handed a measure, which is root cause 3. src/daemon/db/pool.ts:131-136 shares `entry.building` between callers, so abandoning the wait does not start a second connection attempt. [files: src/analyze/measure.ts, src/analyze/context/driver.ts, src/daemon/db/pool.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.2","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The design leaves out nothing from the ISSUE's second fix intent: 'a file or a symbol scope does not cause every entity of its repository to be read'.","evidence":"The design narrows only the measure's own read (measureStoredArea, measure.ts:344). On the production path the same request still reads every entity of the repository: measureRequestScope resolves through resolveTaskScope (measure.ts:294), which for code and docs calls ensureNonEmptyClosure (task-scope.ts:73-74), which does `await listEntitiesForRepo(null, best.path)` and only reads `.length` (invariants.ts:234-237). The design states this one read openly and defers it to ISSUE-61045de91faef1a0, so its own accounting ('one whole-repository read where it causes two today') is correct per call of measureRequestScope. It is still a part of the fix intent that is not delivered. Two further whole-repository reads in the same run are not mentioned: the builder's own `ensureNonEmptyClosure(scope)` for a code run (context/driver.ts:379-380) and the run driver's `resolveTaskScope(intent.scopeRef, intent.target, 'the run')` before planning (orchestrator/driver.ts:368-370). A symbol scope also pays a full entity-table scan while it is resolved (`deps.findEntitiesByFile(filePath)`, context/scope.ts:205), before any measure is taken. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/shared/task-scope.ts, src/analyze/context/invariants.ts, src/analyze/context/driver.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts, src/analyze/context/scope.ts]","action":"No code change to the design is needed if the deferral is accepted. Record the acceptance where the gate reads it: either amend the ISSUE's fix intent and ac4 to say 'the measure's own read is no wider than the scope needs', or have the stakeholder accept this finding with a note that the remaining index-check reads belong to ISSUE-61045de91faef1a0. Add the two other index-check reads (context/driver.ts:380, orchestrator/driver.ts:370) to that issue so its scope is complete.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today a run measures the named area twice: the run driver and the plan RPC each measure, then call buildRunBundle({ intent }, ...), and the builder measures the same resolved scope again for its planning call.","evidence":"src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:317 `const measure = await measureRequestScope(unsized.scopeRef, unsized.target, args.scopeHint);` then 348-350 `shaper.buildRunBundle({ intent }, {...})`. src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:460 `const measure = await measureRequestScope(parsed.intent.scopeRef, parsed.intent.target, parsed.intent.scope);` then 475-476 `shaper.buildRunBundle({ intent }, { runId: parsed.runId })`. src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1373 drops the intent's size (`const { scope: _notRead, ...unsized } = given;`) and 1378 measures: `const area = await (steps.measureArea ?? measureResolvedScope)(args.scope, unsized.target, sizeHint);`. The run driver has a signal (`opts.signal?.aborted`, orchestrator/driver.ts:248) that never reaches the measure. [files: src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts, src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts, src/analyze/context/driver.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The store offers a point read by id and a per-file read; the per-file read has no index and passes over every row of the entity table of all repositories, so a file scope saves only the building of the other files' entities.","evidence":"src/db/entities.ts:585-593 getEntity: `store.entityIdByString.get(id)` then `readEntityRow(store, u64)`, no range scan. 795-811 findEntitiesByFile: `for (const { key, value } of store.entity.getRange())`, decodes each row, resolves its repo path and compares `toAbsolutePath(row.filePath, repoPath) !== file`; it takes no repository argument, so rows of every repository are visited. The design's modest statement of the saving is right for a further reason it does not give: listEntitiesForRepo (779-793) also walks `store.entity.getRange()` over the whole table and decodes every row, skipping only on `row.repoId !== repoId`. So neither read avoids the table scan today; the narrow read saves the id lookup and entity construction for the repository's other files. [files: src/db/entities.ts]","action":"None. When building, keep the comment on the file read honest about this (both reads scan the table until ISSUE-61045de91faef1a0).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The list of callers is complete: buildRunBundle has exactly three production callers (run driver, plan RPC, bundle RPC), and the measuring functions' other callers (classify RPC, freeform probe, analyze-step start, recursive planner) are as the design names them.","evidence":"A search of src/ outside __tests__ for `buildRunBundle(` gives orchestrator/driver.ts:348, daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:295 (buildRun: passes `{ intent, sizeHint? }` as it is) and daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:475 (plan), and no other. Callers of the measure: orchestrator/driver.ts:317, planner/recursive.ts:140, daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:348 (classify) and 460 (plan), explore/freeform-probe.ts:92-93, mcp/analyze-step/phases/start.ts:69 (measureResolvedScope, no builder call), context/driver.ts:1378. PlanBuilderOpts has no `signal` today and RunShapeInput has no `measure` (context/types.ts:183 ends at `sizeHint`), so both are true field additions. The catalog group 'Analysis & memory' exists (config-catalog.ts:87, 89) and the model reader is at mcp/code-review-step/handler.ts:106-113 (`JSON.parse(readFileSync(PATHS.config, 'utf8'))`, fail-safe). [files: src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts, src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts, src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts, src/analyze/explore/freeform-probe.ts, src/mcp/analyze-step/phases/start.ts, src/config/analyze.ts]","action":"One point to carry into the build: the design places the setting's reader in src/config/analyze.ts and requires it to be read each time, not cached. loadAnalyzeConfig there is cached for the daemon's lifetime (`let cached` at 217, returned at 262-263). The reader must be a separate function that reads the file itself, as readFreshnessTimeoutMs does; it must not be a field of AnalyzeConfig.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"For a symbol or file scope the narrow read, kept to entities of the scope's repository, gives the same items, files and size as narrowing the whole-repository read with inAreaOf.","evidence":"src/analyze/runtimes/shared/task-scope.ts:102-103: `if (scope.kind === 'symbol') return e => e.id === scope.entityId;` and `if (scope.kind === 'file') return e => e.file === scope.filePath;`. measureNamedArea (measure.ts:153-168) counts the entities of `scope.repoPath` that pass that test and adds `e.file` to the file set only when it is not empty, which is the design's 'files 1 (0 when the entity has no file path)'. Entity.file is built as `toAbsolutePath(row.filePath, repoRoot)` (entities.ts:122), the same expression findEntitiesByFile compares with its argument (entities.ts:805), so the file read returns exactly the rows whose Entity.file equals scope.filePath, across repositories; the design's filter to the scope's repository removes the others. Entity ids are unique keys (`entityIdByString`), so getEntity plus a check of `repo === scope.repoPath` equals the symbol filter. The fallback to the whole-repository read when the narrow read finds nothing keeps `the repository ... holds no stored entity` (measure.ts:345-348) and the count of 0 for an indexed repository. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/shared/task-scope.ts, src/analyze/measure.ts, src/db/entities.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The bundle cache key does not depend on the size or the stated size today, and adding a handed measure to the input does not change it.","evidence":"src/analyze/context/driver.ts:555-560: keyedInputs returns `{ intent: unsized }` for a run input, built from the intent alone after `const { scope: _size, ...unsized } = intent;`. It is an allow-list: any other field of RunShapeInput, `sizeHint` today and `measure` after the change, is not in the key without any edit to this function. The cache is read before the pipeline (driver.ts:360-367, `readBundle(runId, cacheKey, ...)`), so on a hit no measure is taken with or without a handed one, as today. [files: src/analyze/context/driver.ts]","action":"None. The design's step 'leave it out of the bundle cache key' needs no code in keyedInputs; the test of the key is still worth having because it guards the allow-list.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The seams the design's tests rely on exist, and each acceptance criterion's test would fail on today's code.","evidence":"ac1/ac2/ac3: src/analyze/__tests__/measure-pass.test.ts already stands pools and drivers in through `_setDataPoolSourceForTest` (line 266) with drivers given as plain objects (`listTables: async () => ...`, 273, 326, 335), so a listing or an acquire that never settles can be stood in; on today's code such a test does not return (measure.ts:456, 466 await directly), and the options argument does not exist. ac4: MeasureDeps has `listEntities` and `scope` readers (measure.ts:243-252) and the test file already counts reads with them (line 204); today a symbol or file scope calls `readEntities(scope.repoPath)` (measure.ts:344), so a 'listEntities was not called' assertion fails without the fix. ac5: PipelineSteps has `measureArea` (context/driver.ts:1260) and pipeline-outcome.test.ts stands it in (line 141); today the pipeline calls it unconditionally (1378), so 'not called when a measure is handed' fails without the fix. A whole run with a stand-in model over a sandboxed store exists (orchestrator/__tests__/scope-before-plan.test.ts:88-103, the run context builds), so the run-level count of one measure is reachable: today it is two. [files: src/analyze/__tests__/measure-pass.test.ts, src/analyze/context/__tests__/pipeline-outcome.test.ts, src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/scope-before-plan.test.ts, src/analyze/measure.ts]","action":"Two cautions for the build. (1) Without the fix the ac1 and ac2 tests hang instead of failing an assertion; give each a short per-test timeout so the falsifying run fails fast and visibly. (2) The run-level ac5 test must count a reader that only the measure uses (`listEntities` of MeasureDeps), not the scope readers' `listEntitiesForRepo`, which the index checks call several times in a run (task-scope.ts:74, context/driver.ts:380, orchestrator/driver.ts:370) and would hide the difference.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-10T13:43:54.725Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
